Load decks of sp_diode against ngspice-45, written by ../load.py diode_load.
Builds on PATH: ngspice-45 jfngv2gd3zvi5cmr9vrqfhnziipqd09n (source hfvpfb0bgw9819wkb7kzpdaasbd0hd5r, devices/dio),
VACASK dhxz6l3iac3r2b8n91kcz04a0j3hs4s6 (devices/spice/diode.va, ngspice-47-159 vadng-pre-48).
Run: `nix develop .#testing -c tests/fixtures/families/load_run.sh diode_load`. i(vd) in A, |i(vd)| at 1 GHz for acg/acd.
nom is 27 C, m=1, the control of m3 (27 C, m=3) and of off (80 C, m=3); all give area=2 (level 1, no sidewall: R91 F22's
knee never stands). Regions (vd): rev -2, fwd 0.6, high 0.85 (ikf, rs), bkdn -5.2 (bv=5). acd only (two terminals).
Oracles (fd.py, last lines): each nominal region's operating point moved 1e-5 V on the gate (base) and the drain
(collector, anode), whose central differences are gm and gds of the DC law, against |i(vd)| at 1 kHz; it holds where
the conductance is well above the 1 kHz capacitive current and the differences' resolution (ngspice prints 12 digits:
about 5e-11 S), so not in cutoff or reverse. And the multiplier's metamorphic relation: every m3 reading is 3 times its
nom reading within 1e-9 relative and 1e-10 absolute (the solver's gmin is not multiplied); a failing row is printed.
The model gives isr=1e-12 nr=2 (the recombination current), ikf, rs, bv/ibv, cjo/vj/m/fc, tt, xti, eg.
Result: two differences, both in the recombination current; the control ../diode_noisr (the same cards without isr
and nr) agrees everywhere (DC to 6e-5 at a reverse pA, AC to 1e-10, both AC the derivatives).
(1) Reverse DC: ngspice-45 carries no recombination current under reverse bias, VACASK does: nom_rev_dc 2.020e-12 A
against 3.679e-12 (the gmin and is*area parts agree; without isr both read 2.020e-12), off_rev_dc 4.60e-11 against
2.08e-10. Class: a law (R90 shape), carried by a diode whose model gives isr, at a reverse bias.
(2) Forward AC: ngspice-45's conductance at nom_fwd (0.6 V, recombination-dominated) is 7.66e-5 off the central
difference of its own DC current, 1.2e-6 at nom_high; VACASK 2e-8. At 1 GHz fwd 3.3e-5. Class: ngspice-45's AC is
not its DC law's linearisation (as mos2/3/9 and bjt).
Rechecked 2026-11-13 under R91b (../../checked.sh: a run whose exit status is not 0 or whose output says it aborted, stepped too small or met a singular matrix gives refused(<why>), never a reading): every reading reproduced.

